<comment pinned="false">Hold B while switching on for demo timings: 10 s waits and a 1 minute sunscreen timer.
Hold A for show mode: demo timings, pretend UV values that climb through every band, and
alerts that answer themselves, so the device performs the whole flowchart on its own</comment>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">----- Device turns on -----</comment>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">USB link speed: 1 = normal (115200), 2 = slow (9600). Use 2 if the app says lines
arrive damaged, and choose 9600 in the app's Tools as well</comment>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">Safety limits: how long an alert beeps before giving up, and how long a
value from the phone counts as "the phone is sending online UV"</comment>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">Timings from the flowchart</comment>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">UV bands from the flowchart (WHO scale), tested on the rounded UV index:
0-2 low, 3-7 moderate / high, 8-10 very high, 11+ extreme</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">I2C address: 60 = 0x3C (usual), 61 = 0x3D</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">1 = SSD1306 (most 0.96" screens), 2 = SH1106 (most 1.3" screens)</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">OLED screen on the I2C pins (optional).  0 = no screen, 1 = detect it, 2 = always on</comment>
</block>
</next>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">Angles for a positional servo: resting, and the tap</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">Servo on P2: 1 = normal positional servo, 2 = continuous rotation servo</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">How loud the beeps are, 0-255 (the app can change it for one session with vol=)</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">Sound: 1 = micro:bit V2 speaker, 2 = buzzer on P0 (a V1 always uses P0)</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">One reading is the middle value of this many samples (kills noise spikes)</comment>
</block>
</next>
<comment pinned="false">UV sensor on P1.  1 = GUVA-S12SD / Crowtail / Grove / DFRobot / ElecFreaks
2 = ML8511 (SparkFun, Adafruit)   3 = sensors sold as "0-1023 = UV 0-15"</comment>
</block>
</statement>
