<comment pinned="false">The flowchart from top to bottom. Every box and decision is a function below,
named after the box. "A and B held?" is the A+B button block: it turns the
device off at any moment; every wait stops as soon as that happens and the
rest of the trip is skipped. A branch that ended in standby goes straight
back to "Read UV sensor" instead of waiting 5 minutes.</comment>
</block>
<block id="!I4fWJ:6r,+]QRHLYNmG" type="function_definition" x="2564" y="266">
<mutation name="readUvSensor">
</mutation>
<statement name="STACK">
<block id="(F=7c#+02,xZ6}%j@)uy" type="variables_set">
<field name="VAR">stateName</field>
<value name="VALUE">
<shadow type="math_number"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow>
<block type="text">
<field name="TEXT">reading</field>
</block>
</value>
<next>
